From 3bfe2416fa9254cf8791acbf4c260972c674f1d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:40:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [TransferEngine][ROCm] HipGemAllocator: pin through the
 first NIC that takes the MR; review fixes

- The one-page dma-buf pin stopped at the first RDMA device that allocated a
  protection domain, so a device that then rejected the dma-buf MR failed
  every allocation even when another device would pin it. pickPinDevice()
  (hip_gem_pin.h) now tries the device that pinned the last buffer first and
  then the others, and a device becomes preferred only once a pin on it
  succeeds. hip_gem_pin_test covers it without a GPU or RDMA device.
- Finding the allocator is a dlsym() over every loaded library. The device
  lookups on per-transfer paths (the HIP transport's copy device, the TCP
  transport's staging device) only use an allocator a registration already
  found, so processes without HipGemAllocator pay nothing per transfer.
- mc_hip_gem_malloc() rejects a non-positive size.
- hip_gem_allocator_test polls the transfer status with a 1 ms sleep and a
  60 s limit instead of spinning.
- Quote the paths build_wheel.sh copies; glob the render node as render*.

Signed-off-by: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
